I inlined the `GetField` duplicate scan directly into `AddField` (avoiding a potential non-inlined call and pointer indirection) and pre-reserve a small capacity on the first insertion, eliminating the repeated geometric reallocations/copies that occur while fields are added one-by-one per message.

```cpp
void Mesg::AddField(const Field& field)
{
    const auto num = field.GetNum();
    for (const Field& f : fields)
    {
        if (f.GetNum() == num)
            return;
    }
    if (fields.empty())
        fields.reserve(16);
    fields.push_back(field);
}
```